[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix. The reports say otherwise. We merged them
on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and every one of them
has a subject about a wrong date, so <Count ticket={4471} of="problems" /> different problems
went into one ticket. Each now has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes <Count ticket={4471} of="parser" /> reports. It does not touch the
<Count ticket={4471} of="hint" /> from the booking-v3 form or the <Count ticket={4471} of="shift" />
that moved by one day.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## How to tell them apart

Not by subject: all three share the same subject lines. Not by intake's tag: it guesses from
the reporter's browser, not from the tenant. Look at the tenant, the way in, and the body.

- **`parser`**: a day-first tenant, by app, email or the booking-v2 form. The body names two dates
  with day and month swapped: "8 December is now 12 August".
- **`hint`**: a booking-v3 tenant (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour), by the form. The
  body looks the same as `parser`, but the hint under the date field told the person to type month
  first. Fixing the parser leaves this one as it is; the form's hint or its reading has to change.
- **`shift`**: the date moves by one day, or differs between two places: "Client in Lisbon got
  Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." No month swap explains it. The desk had already noted
  these (desk notes, `oneDayMove`) and still counted them under `parser`.

## Counting

The export comes in overlapping pages: <Count ticket={4471} of="rows" /> rows hold
<Count ticket={4471} of="unique" /> reports. Each report is counted once, under one problem.

## For the desk

- Before you merge into a big ticket, check that the cause matches, not just the subject. The
  explorer on [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows the cause for each pair.
- When a desk note says some reports read differently, give them a ticket of their own, not a footnote.

